                    '三日慶典被視為一個連貫的慶典，在復活主日晚禱結束。' ],
                   en: [
                    'Holy Week begins on Palm Sunday with the reading of the Passion.',
                    'Holy Thursday evening, Mass of the Lord\'s Supper: remembering the institution of the Eucharist and the priesthood, with the washing of the feet.',
                    'Good Friday, the Lord\'s Passion: no Mass is celebrated; the Passion is read, the cross is venerated and Communion is given.',
                    'Holy Saturday night, Easter Vigil: the service of light (Paschal candle), the Liturgy of the Word, baptisms, then the Liturgy of the Eucharist, the greatest celebration of the year.',
                    'The Triduum is treated as one continuous celebration and ends with Evening Prayer on Easter Sunday.' ] },
              k: '聖週 棕枝 聖枝 聖週四 聖週五 受難 復活夜 守夜 洗腳 triduum holy week palm sunday holy thursday good friday easter vigil washing feet' },

            { id: 'year-easter', cat: 'year', icon: 'fa-sun',
              t: { zh: '復活期', en: 'Easter Season' },
              s: { zh: '從復活主日到聖神降臨主日，共五十天的喜樂。',
                   en: 'Fifty days of joy from Easter Sunday to Pentecost.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '顏色為白色；聖神降臨主日用紅色。',
                    '復活蠟象徵復活的基督是世界的光，在復活期的彌撒中點燃。',
                    '復活夜及復活主日，信友重發聖洗誓願，記起自己的洗禮。',
                    '期間包括基督升天與聖神降臨，到聖神降臨主日圓滿結束。' ],
                   en: [
                    'The color is white; red on Pentecost Sunday.',
                    'The Paschal candle, a sign of the risen Christ as the light of the world, is lit at Masses throughout the season.',
                    'At the Easter Vigil and on Easter Sunday the faithful renew their baptismal promises.',
                    'The season includes the Ascension of the Lord and ends with Pentecost.' ] },
              k: '復活期 復活節 復活蠟 聖神降臨 升天 easter season paschal candle pentecost ascension' },

            { id: 'year-ordinary', cat: 'year', icon: 'fa-seedling',
              t: { zh: '常年期', en: 'Ordinary Time' },
              s: { zh: '「常年」是「按次序編號」的意思，不是「平凡」；一年中有 33 或 34 個星期。',
                   en: '“Ordinary” means “numbered in order”, not “plain”. It covers 33 or 34 weeks of the year.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '顏色為綠色，象徵生命的成長。',
                    '這段時間不特別慶祝基督奧蹟的某一個層面，而是按週回顧基督的公開生活與教導。',
                    '主日福音按 A、B、C 年輪流誦讀瑪竇、馬爾谷、路加福音。',
                    '常年期是日常生活中跟隨基督、持續成長的時期。' ],
                   en: [
                    'The color is green, a sign of growing life.',
                    'The season does not highlight one aspect of Christ\'s mystery but follows his public life and teaching week by week.',
                    'Sunday Gospels run through Matthew, Mark and Luke in Years A, B and C.',
                    'It is the time for following Christ and growing steadily in everyday life.' ] },
              k: '常年期 綠色 ordinary time green weeks' },

            { id: 'year-ranks', cat: 'year', icon: 'fa-ranking-star',
              t: { zh: '禮儀日的等級', en: 'Ranks of Liturgical Days' },
              s: { zh: '禮儀曆中的日子分為節日、慶日、紀念及自由紀念。',
                   en: 'Days in the liturgical calendar are ranked as solemnities, feasts, memorials and optional memorials.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '節日（Solemnity）：最高等級，如聖誕節、復活節、聖母升天、大聖若瑟（3 月 19 日）；通常有光榮頌及信經。',
                    '慶日（Feast）：次一等級，如各位宗徒的慶日、主受洗節。',
                    '紀念（Memorial）：紀念聖人，如聖多瑪斯・亞奎那；自由紀念則可選擇是否慶祝。',
                    '中文譯名各地略有不同（例如舊稱「瞻禮」），請以教區禮儀年曆為準。' ],
                   en: [
                    'Solemnity: the highest rank, such as Christmas, Easter, the Assumption and St. Joseph (19 March); usually with the Gloria and the Creed.',
                    'Feast: the next rank, such as feasts of the Apostles and the Baptism of the Lord.',
                    'Memorial: remembers a saint; an optional memorial may be celebrated or not.',
                    'Chinese terms vary a little by region (older texts use “瞻禮”); follow your diocesan calendar.' ] },
              k: '節日 慶日 紀念 瞻禮 自由紀念 等級 solemnity feast memorial optional rank' },

            // ---------- SACRAMENTS ----------
            { id: 'sacr-seven', cat: 'sacr', icon: 'fa-droplet',
              t: { zh: '七件聖事', en: 'The Seven Sacraments' },
              s: { zh: '聖事是基督建立的有效標記，把天主的恩寵賜給我們。',
                   en: 'The sacraments are effective signs instituted by Christ that give us God\'s grace.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '入門聖事：聖洗、堅振、聖體。',
                    '治療聖事：和好（告解）、病人傅油。',
                    '服務共融的聖事：聖秩、婚姻。',
                    '聖體聖事是整個基督徒生活的泉源與高峰。' ],
                   en: [
                    'Sacraments of Initiation: Baptism, Confirmation, Eucharist.',
                    'Sacraments of Healing: Reconciliation (Confession) and Anointing of the Sick.',
                    'Sacraments at the service of communion: Holy Orders and Matrimony.',
                    'The Eucharist is the source and summit of Christian life.' ] },
              k: '七件聖事 聖事 聖洗 堅振 聖體 告解 傅油 聖秩 婚配 seven sacraments baptism confirmation holy orders matrimony' },

            { id: 'sacr-confession', cat: 'sacr', icon: 'fa-hand-holding-heart',
              t: { zh: '告解（和好聖事）', en: 'Confession (Reconciliation)' },
              s: { zh: '天主藉司鐸赦免我們的罪，使我們與天主及教會重修舊好。',
                   en: 'Through the priest, God forgives our sins and reconciles us with himself and the Church.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '步驟：省察良心 → 痛悔 → 向司鐸告明 → 領受補贖 → 聽司鐸念赦罪經並完成補贖。',
                    '聽告解的司鐸負有嚴格的告解保密責任。',
                    '犯了大罪後，領聖體前必須先辦告解；教會要求至少每年一次。',
                    '定期告解（例如每月或每個四旬期、將臨期）能幫助我們持續悔改。' ],
                   en: [
                    'Steps: examine your conscience → be sorry → confess to the priest → receive a penance → hear the words of absolution and complete the penance.',
                    'The priest is bound by the strict seal of confession.',
                    'After serious sin, go to Confession before receiving Communion; the Church asks for confession at least once a year.',
                    'Regular confession (for example monthly, or in Lent and Advent) helps us keep growing in conversion.' ] },
              k: '告解 和好 補贖 省察 痛悔 赦罪 大罪 懺悔 confession reconciliation penance absolution sin examination of conscience' },

            { id: 'sacr-baptism', cat: 'sacr', icon: 'fa-water',
              t: { zh: '聖洗聖事', en: 'Baptism' },
              s: { zh: '藉水與「因父及子及聖神之名」，成為天主的子女和教會的成員。',
                   en: 'With water and the words “in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit”, we become God\'s children and members of the Church.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '洗去原罪及洗前所犯的罪，賜予新生命，是進入教會及領受其他聖事的門徑。',
                    '成人經由「成人入門聖事」（慕道期）領洗；嬰孩由父母帶領，並有教父母協助。',
                    '教父母須是已領洗、堅振並過著與信仰相稱生活的天主教徒。',
                    '緊急時（如有死亡危險），任何人只要有意願行教會所做的，用水並唸出三位一體的聖名，也可以施洗。' ],
                   en: [
                    'It washes away original sin and any sin committed before baptism, gives new life, and is the gateway to the Church and the other sacraments.',
                    'Adults are baptized after a period of formation (the catechumenate); infants are brought by their parents with the help of godparents.',
                    'Godparents must be baptized and confirmed Catholics who live lives in keeping with the faith.',
                    'In an emergency (danger of death) anyone with the intention to do what the Church does may baptize, pouring water and saying the Trinitarian formula.' ] },
              k: '聖洗 洗禮 領洗 教父 教母 嬰孩 成人 慕道 baptism godparents catechumen rcia water' },

            { id: 'sacr-marriage', cat: 'sacr', icon: 'fa-ring',
              t: { zh: '婚姻聖事', en: 'Matrimony' },
              s: { zh: '一男一女以終身不渝的盟約結合，彼此扶持並開放生命。',
                   en: 'A man and a woman join in a lifelong covenant, supporting one another and open to life.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '夫妻二人彼此授予婚姻聖事，司鐸或執事代表教會見證並降福。',
                    '特質：忠貞、不可拆散、開放生育並教養子女。',
                    '教會鼓勵婚前參加輔導課程，並在婚姻生活中持續成長。',
                    '作丈夫與父親，可以學習大聖若瑟的守護與責任。' ],
                   en: [
                    'The spouses confer the sacrament on each other; the priest or deacon witnesses on behalf of the Church and gives the blessing.',
                    'Its marks are fidelity, indissolubility, openness to children and their upbringing.',
                    'The Church encourages marriage preparation and continued growth in married life.',
                    'Husbands and fathers can learn from St. Joseph\'s care and responsibility.' ] },
              k: '婚姻 婚配 夫妻 丈夫 父親 忠貞 matrimony marriage husband father spouse wedding' },

            { id: 'sacr-anointing', cat: 'sacr', icon: 'fa-heart-pulse',
              t: { zh: '病人傅油', en: 'Anointing of the Sick' },
              s: { zh: '為病重或年老體弱者而設，帶來天主的安慰、力量與平安。',
                   en: 'For those who are seriously ill or frail with age; it brings God\'s comfort, strength and peace.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '不只是臨終才領受；病情嚴重、手術前或年老體弱時都可以請求。',
                    '由司鐸（或主教）以聖油傅抹額頭與雙手，並誦念祈禱。',
                    '同一個人在病情惡化時可再次領受。',
                    '臨終時，聖體稱為「臨終聖體」（Viaticum），是前往天父的旅途食糧。' ],
                   en: [
                    'It is not only for the dying: it may be requested in serious illness, before major surgery or in frailty due to age.',
                    'A priest (or bishop) anoints the forehead and hands with blessed oil and prays.',
                    'The same person may receive it again if the illness worsens.',
                    'At the point of death, Communion is called Viaticum: food for the journey to the Father.' ] },
              k: '傅油 病人 聖油 臨終 病重 年老 anointing sick oil viaticum illness elderly' },

            // ---------- PRAYER & DEVOTIONS ----------
            { id: 'prayer-cross', cat: 'prayer', icon: 'fa-cross',
              t: { zh: '聖號經與畫十字', en: 'The Sign of the Cross' },
              s: { zh: '「因父及子及聖神之名。亞孟。」是最簡短的信仰宣認。',
                   en: '“In the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit. Amen.” is the shortest profession of faith.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '用右手由額頭到胸前，再由左肩到右肩，表示相信聖三及基督的十字架。',
                    '祈禱、彌撒、飲食前後和一天的開始與結束，都可以畫十字聖號。',
                    '進入聖堂時用聖水畫十字，提醒我們的洗禮。',
                    '在福音前，也在額頭、口唇和心前畫小十字，求主使我們的思想、言語與內心都屬於祂。' ],
                   en: [
                    'With the right hand, touch the forehead, then the chest, then the left and right shoulders, professing faith in the Trinity and in Christ\'s cross.',
                    'Make it at prayer, at Mass, before and after meals, and at the beginning and end of the day.',
                    'On entering a church, sign yourself with holy water to recall your baptism.',
                    'Before the Gospel, we trace a small cross on forehead, lips and heart, asking that our thoughts, words and heart belong to him.' ] },
              k: '聖號 十字 聖水 畫十字 sign of the cross holy water trinity' },

            { id: 'prayer-rosary', cat: 'prayer', icon: 'fa-circle-dot',
              t: { zh: '玫瑰經', en: 'The Rosary' },
              s: { zh: '藉聖母的伴隨默想基督的生平，是廣受愛戴的民間敬禮。',
                   en: 'A well-loved devotion that meditates on the life of Christ with Mary at our side.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '每「端」默想一件奧蹟，唸 1 遍天主經、10 遍聖母經和 1 遍聖三光榮頌；一串玫瑰經共五端。',
                    '四組奧蹟：喜樂、痛苦、榮福與光明（光明五端由教宗若望保祿二世於 2002 年加入）。',
                    '一般安排：星期一、六—喜樂；星期二、五—痛苦；星期三、日—榮福；星期四—光明。',
                    '五月是聖母月，十月是玫瑰月；10 月 7 日是玫瑰聖母紀念日。' ],
                   en: [
                    'Each decade meditates on one mystery, with 1 Our Father, 10 Hail Marys and 1 Glory Be; a full rosary has five decades.',
                    'There are four sets of mysteries: Joyful, Sorrowful, Glorious and Luminous (the Luminous Mysteries were added by Pope John Paul II in 2002).',
                    'Usual arrangement: Monday and Saturday, Joyful; Tuesday and Friday, Sorrowful; Wednesday and Sunday, Glorious; Thursday, Luminous.',
                    'May is the month of Mary and October is the month of the Rosary; 7 October is Our Lady of the Rosary.' ] },
              k: '玫瑰經 聖母經 五端 奧蹟 喜樂 痛苦 榮福 光明 玫瑰月 rosary hail mary mysteries decade joyful sorrowful glorious luminous october' },

            { id: 'prayer-hours', cat: 'prayer', icon: 'fa-clock',
              t: { zh: '日課（時辰頌禱）', en: 'Liturgy of the Hours' },
              s: { zh: '教會的公共祈禱，以聖詠聖化一天的時辰。',
                   en: 'The public prayer of the Church, sanctifying the hours of the day with the psalms.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '主要時辰：晨禱與晚禱，是一天祈禱的「樞紐」。',
                    '其他時辰：誦讀日課、日間祈禱（午前、午時、午後）和夜禱。',
                    '平信徒也被鼓勵參與，可獨自、與家人或在小組中誦念。',
                    '祈禱以聖詠為主，加上聖經及教父的誦讀、短答禱和禱詞。' ],
                   en: [
                    'The two main hours, Morning Prayer and Evening Prayer, are the hinges of the day\'s prayer.',
                    'The other hours are the Office of Readings, Daytime Prayer (mid-morning, midday, mid-afternoon) and Night Prayer.',
                    'Lay people are encouraged to join in: alone, with family or in a small group.',
                    'The prayer centers on the Psalms, with readings from Scripture and the Fathers, responsories and prayers.' ] },
              k: '日課 時辰頌禱 晨禱 晚禱 夜禱 聖詠 liturgy of the hours divine office morning evening night prayer psalms breviary' },

            { id: 'prayer-adoration', cat: 'prayer', icon: 'fa-sun',
              t: { zh: '聖體朝拜與聖體降福', en: 'Eucharistic Adoration & Benediction' },
              s: { zh: '在彌撒以外，欽崇留在聖體內的耶穌。',
                   en: 'Worshipping Jesus present in the Eucharist outside Mass.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '聖體可供奉在聖體櫃，或顯示於聖體光（顯供）中，讓信友朝拜。',
                    '朝拜時可默禱、誦念聖詠、讀聖經或唸玫瑰經，靜靜與主同在。',
                    '「聖體降福」由司鐸或執事以聖體光向會眾降福，並以讚美聖體的歌詠與祈禱。',
                    '聖體朝拜源自彌撒，並引領我們回到彌撒。' ],
                   en: [
                    'The Blessed Sacrament may be reserved in the tabernacle, or exposed in a monstrance for adoration.',
                    'In adoration we may pray silently, read the Psalms or Scripture, or pray the rosary, simply being with the Lord.',
                    'In Benediction the priest or deacon blesses the people with the monstrance, with hymns and prayers praising the Eucharist.',
                    'Adoration flows from the Mass and leads us back to it.' ] },
              k: '聖體朝拜 聖體降福 聖體光 聖體櫃 朝拜 默禱 adoration benediction monstrance tabernacle holy hour' },

            { id: 'prayer-forms', cat: 'prayer', icon: 'fa-hands-praying',
              t: { zh: '祈禱的五種形式', en: 'Five Forms of Prayer' },
              s: { zh: '《天主教教理》介紹的五種基本祈禱形式。',
                   en: 'The five basic forms of prayer described in the Catechism of the Catholic Church.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '讚頌與欽崇：承認天主是創造者與救主，單單因為祂是天主。',
                    '祈求：向天主陳明自己的需要，包括求寬恕。',
                    '代禱：為別人祈求，如為家人、同事與團體。',
                    '感恩：為天主的恩賜和一切事情感謝祂。',
                    '讚美：因天主是天主而歡呼，不求任何回報。' ],
                   en: [
                    'Blessing and adoration: acknowledging God as Creator and Savior simply because he is God.',
                    'Petition: bringing our needs to God, including asking forgiveness.',
                    'Intercession: praying for others, such as family, colleagues and our community.',
                    'Thanksgiving: thanking God for his gifts and for all things.',
                    'Praise: rejoicing in God for who he is, asking nothing in return.' ] },
              k: '祈禱 形式 讚頌 欽崇 祈求 代禱 感恩 讚美 教理 forms of prayer blessing petition intercession thanksgiving praise catechism how to pray' },

            { id: 'prayer-lectio', cat: 'prayer', icon: 'fa-book-bible',
              t: { zh: '神讀（Lectio Divina）', en: 'Lectio Divina' },
              s: { zh: '以祈禱的心緩慢誦讀聖經，適合個人及小組分享。',
                   en: 'Praying with Scripture by reading slowly and prayerfully; suitable for individuals and small groups.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '誦讀（Lectio）：慢慢讀一段經文，留意打動你的字句。',
                    '默想（Meditatio）：思考天主透過這段話向我說什麼。',
                    '祈禱（Oratio）：用自己的話回應天主，感謝、求助或悔改。',
                    '默觀（Contemplatio）：靜默片刻，安息在天主臨在中。',
                    '行動（Actio）：定一個今天可以實踐的小行動。' ],
                   en: [
                    'Lectio (read): slowly read a passage and notice the words that stand out.',
                    'Meditatio (reflect): ask what God is saying to me through these words.',
                    'Oratio (pray): respond in your own words with thanks, petition or repentance.',
                    'Contemplatio (rest): be silent for a moment, resting in God\'s presence.',
                    'Actio (act): choose one small action to live out today.' ] },
              k: '神讀 聖言誦讀 默想 默觀 聖經 小組 lectio divina scripture meditation contemplation bible study' },

            // ---------- CHURCH & SACRED OBJECTS ----------
            { id: 'space-church', cat: 'space', icon: 'fa-place-of-worship',
              t: { zh: '聖堂的主要部分', en: 'Main Parts of a Church' },
              s: { zh: '聖堂內的每個位置，都指向基督與禮儀的奧蹟。',
                   en: 'Every place in the church points to Christ and the mystery of the liturgy.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '祭台：象徵基督，是舉行祭獻的地方，也是信友共聚的聖筵。',
                    '讀經台（誦讀台）：宣讀天主聖言的地方。',
                    '司鐸座：主祭司鐸在彌撒中主持禮儀的座位。',
                    '聖體櫃與聖體燈：保存聖體；聖體燈常明，表示基督臨在。',
                    '聖水盆、苦路及聖像：幫助信友祈禱與默想。' ],
                   en: [
                    'Altar: a sign of Christ, the place of the sacrifice, and the table around which the faithful gather.',
                    'Ambo (lectern): the place from which God\'s Word is proclaimed.',
                    'Presider\'s chair: where the priest presides over the celebration.',
                    'Tabernacle and sanctuary lamp: the tabernacle reserves the Blessed Sacrament; the lamp burns continually to signal Christ\'s presence.',
                    'Holy water font, Stations of the Cross and images: aids to prayer and meditation.' ] },
              k: '聖堂 祭台 讀經台 司鐸座 聖體櫃 聖體燈 聖水盆 church altar ambo tabernacle sanctuary lamp holy water font stations' },

            { id: 'space-vessels', cat: 'space', icon: 'fa-wine-glass',
              t: { zh: '彌撒用具', en: 'Mass Vessels & Linens' },
              s: { zh: '用於聖祭禮儀的聖器與布巾，都以恭敬與整潔的態度對待。',
                   en: 'The vessels and linens used in the Eucharistic liturgy are treated with reverence and care.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '聖爵：盛載祝聖後成為基督聖血的酒。',
                    '聖盤與聖體盒：盛放聖體。',
                    '聖體布：鋪在祭台上，承接聖體；聖爵巾用於擦拭聖爵。',
                    '彌撒經本、讀經集與福音書：宣讀禱詞與聖言所用的經書。' ],
                   en: [
                    'Chalice: holds the wine that becomes the Blood of Christ.',
                    'Paten and ciborium: hold the hosts, which become the Body of Christ.',
                    'Corporal: a cloth spread on the altar to receive the sacred vessels; the purificator is used to cleanse the chalice.',
                    'Missal, Lectionary and Book of the Gospels: the books used for the prayers and the proclamation of the Word.' ] },
              k: '聖爵 聖盤 聖體盒 聖體布 聖爵巾 經本 chalice paten ciborium corporal purificator missal lectionary vessels' },

