                    'On 8 December 2020 Pope Francis issued the apostolic letter Patris Corde (“With a Father\'s Heart”) and proclaimed a Year of St. Joseph.',
                    'Scripture records no word he spoke, yet he obeyed God in action and protected the Holy Family, a model for men.' ] },
              k: '若瑟 聖若瑟 勞工 父親 主保 養父 聖家 joseph patron worker father holy family patris corde' },

            { id: 'saint-peter', cat: 'saints', icon: 'fa-mountain',
              t: { zh: '伯多祿與「磐石」', en: 'St. Peter and “the Rock”' },
              s: { zh: 'Petros 是希臘文的「磐石」，耶穌賜給西滿的新名字。',
                   en: '“Petros” is Greek for “rock”, the new name Jesus gave to Simon.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '瑪竇福音 16:18：「你是伯多祿，在這磐石上我要建立我的教會。」',
                    '伯多祿是十二宗徒之首，也曾軟弱否認主，卻在悔改中成為堅固弟兄的磐石。',
                    '6 月 29 日是聖伯多祿聖保祿宗徒節日；2 月 22 日是「伯多祿宗座」慶日。',
                    '這也是「磐石」團體的名字：把生命建在基督身上，並彼此堅固。' ],
                   en: [
                    'Matthew 16:18: “You are Peter, and on this rock I will build my Church.”',
                    'Peter was the first among the Twelve. He also failed and denied the Lord, yet through repentance became a rock to strengthen his brothers.',
                    '29 June is the solemnity of Sts. Peter and Paul; 22 February is the feast of the Chair of St. Peter.',
                    'It is also the name of our group: to build our lives on Christ and strengthen one another.' ] },
              k: '伯多祿 彼得 磐石 磐石團體 petros peter rock apostle simon keys' },

            { id: 'saint-mary', cat: 'saints', icon: 'fa-crown',
              t: { zh: '聖母的主要節日', en: 'Main Feasts of Mary' },
              s: { zh: '天主教徒敬愛聖母，因為她是耶穌的母親，也是我們的母親。',
                   en: 'Catholics honor Mary because she is the Mother of Jesus and our mother too.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '1 月 1 日：天主之母聖母節（節日）。',
                    '3 月 25 日：天使向聖母報喜節（節日）。',
                    '8 月 15 日：聖母升天節（節日）。',
                    '12 月 8 日：聖母無染原罪節（節日）。',
                    '5 月（聖母月）與 10 月（玫瑰月）特別敬禮聖母。' ],
                   en: [
                    '1 January: Solemnity of Mary, Mother of God.',
                    '25 March: Solemnity of the Annunciation of the Lord.',
                    '15 August: Solemnity of the Assumption of Mary.',
                    '8 December: Solemnity of the Immaculate Conception.',
                    'May (month of Mary) and October (month of the Rosary) are times of special devotion to her.' ] },
              k: '聖母 瑪利亞 天主之母 報喜 升天 無染原罪 聖母月 mary mother of god annunciation assumption immaculate conception' },

            { id: 'saint-all', cat: 'saints', icon: 'fa-dove',
              t: { zh: '諸聖節與追思節', en: 'All Saints & All Souls' },
              s: { zh: '11 月 1 日紀念所有聖人，11 月 2 日為所有亡者祈禱。',
                   en: '1 November honors all the saints; 2 November is a day of prayer for all the faithful departed.' },
              p: { zh: [
                    '11 月 1 日諸聖節（節日）：慶祝所有已在天堂享見天主的聖人。',
                    '11 月 2 日追思已亡節：為已去世的人祈禱，求天主接納他們。',
                    '11 月傳統上稱為「煉靈月」，教會鼓勵為亡者獻彌撒和祈禱。',
                    '追思亡者的彌撒，司鐸可穿紫色、白色或黑色的祭衣。' ],
                   en: [
                    '1 November, All Saints (solemnity): celebrates all the saints who now see God in heaven.',
                    '2 November, All Souls: we pray for the faithful departed, asking God to receive them.',
                    'November is traditionally the month of the Holy Souls; the Church encourages Masses and prayers for the dead.',
                    'At funeral and All Souls Masses the priest may wear violet, white or black vestments.' ] },
              k: '諸聖節 追思 亡者 煉靈 十一月 殯葬 喪禮 all saints all souls dead funeral november purgatory' }
        ];


        // ===================== SPIRITUAL COMPANION KNOWLEDGE BASE =====================
        // Scripture excerpts (Chinese follows the 思高 Bible style; English is a plain modern rendering).
        // Wording is excerpted for meditation; the chat reminds readers to check the full text.
        const V = {
            is26_4:   { r: ['依撒意亞 26:4', 'Isaiah 26:4'], zh: '你們應永遠信賴上主，因為上主是永固的磐石。', en: 'Trust in the LORD forever! For the LORD is an eternal rock.' },
            ps23_1:   { r: ['聖詠 23:1', 'Psalm 23:1'], zh: '上主是我的牧者，我實在一無所缺。', en: 'The LORD is my shepherd; there is nothing I lack.' },
            phil4_6:  { r: ['斐理伯書 4:6-7', 'Philippians 4:6-7'], zh: '你們什麼也不要憂慮，只要事事以祈禱和懇求，並懷著感謝之心，將你們的願望呈告天主；那麼，出人意外的天主的平安，必在基督耶穌內保守你們的心思念慮。', en: 'Do not be anxious about anything, but in every situation, by prayer and petition, with thanksgiving, present your requests to God. And the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and minds in Christ Jesus.' },
            jos1_9:   { r: ['若蘇厄書 1:9', 'Joshua 1:9'], zh: '你當勇敢堅強，不要害怕，也不要畏懼，因為上主你的天主必與你同在，無論你到哪裡去。', en: 'Be strong and courageous. Do not be afraid or dismayed, for the LORD your God is with you wherever you go.' },
            mt11_28:  { r: ['瑪竇福音 11:28', 'Matthew 11:28'], zh: '凡勞苦和負重擔的，你們都到我跟前來，我要使你們安息。', en: 'Come to me, all you who labor and are burdened, and I will give you rest.' },
            jn14_27:  { r: ['若望福音 14:27', 'John 14:27'], zh: '我將平安留給你們，將我的平安賜給你們；我所賜給你們的，不像世界所賜的一樣。', en: 'Peace I leave with you; my peace I give to you. Not as the world gives do I give it to you.' },
            ps127_1:  { r: ['聖詠 127:1', 'Psalm 127:1'], zh: '若不是上主建造房屋，建築的人就白白勞苦；若不是上主守護城市，守衛的人就白白警醒。', en: 'Unless the LORD builds the house, those who build it labor in vain. Unless the LORD guards the city, the guard keeps watch in vain.' },
            col3_23:  { r: ['哥羅森書 3:23', 'Colossians 3:23'], zh: '無論做什麼，你們要從心裡去做，像為主做的，而不是為人做的。', en: 'Whatever you do, do it from the heart, as for the Lord and not for others.' },
            pt5_7:    { r: ['伯多祿前書 5:7', '1 Peter 5:7'], zh: '你們要把一切憂慮卸給天主，因為他必關心你們。', en: 'Cast all your worries upon him, because he cares for you.' },
            mt6_34:   { r: ['瑪竇福音 6:34', 'Matthew 6:34'], zh: '所以，不要為明天憂慮，因為明天自有明天的憂慮；一天的苦惱，一天擔當就夠了。', en: 'Do not worry about tomorrow; tomorrow will take care of itself. Sufficient for a day is its own evil.' },
            is41_10:  { r: ['依撒意亞 41:10', 'Isaiah 41:10'], zh: '你不要害怕，因為我與你同在；不要驚惶，因為我是你的天主；我必堅固你，必幫助你，必以我正義的右手扶持你。', en: 'Do not fear, for I am with you; do not be anxious, for I am your God. I will strengthen you and help you, I will uphold you with my victorious right hand.' },
            ps27_1:   { r: ['聖詠 27:1', 'Psalm 27:1'], zh: '上主是我的光明，是我的救援，我還害怕誰？上主是我生命的保障，我還懼怕誰？', en: 'The LORD is my light and my salvation; whom should I fear? The LORD is my life\'s refuge; of whom should I be afraid?' },
            eph5_25:  { r: ['厄弗所書 5:25', 'Ephesians 5:25'], zh: '作丈夫的，你們應愛自己的妻子，如同基督愛了教會，並為她捨棄了自己。', en: 'Husbands, love your wives, even as Christ loved the Church and handed himself over for her.' },
            eph6_4:   { r: ['厄弗所書 6:4', 'Ephesians 6:4'], zh: '作父親的，不要激怒你們的兒女，要以主的教訓和勸戒教養他們。', en: 'Fathers, do not provoke your children to anger, but bring them up with the training and instruction of the Lord.' },
            jos24_15: { r: ['若蘇厄書 24:15', 'Joshua 24:15'], zh: '至於我和我的家庭，我們要事奉上主。', en: 'As for me and my household, we will serve the LORD.' },
            jas1_19:  { r: ['雅各伯書 1:19-20', 'James 1:19-20'], zh: '你們每人應該快於聽，慢於說，慢於動怒，因為人的憤怒並不實行天主的正義。', en: 'Everyone should be quick to listen, slow to speak, slow to anger, for the anger of a man does not accomplish the righteousness of God.' },
            eph4_26:  { r: ['厄弗所書 4:26', 'Ephesians 4:26'], zh: '你們即使憤怒，也不要犯罪；不要讓太陽在你們的憤怒中下山。', en: 'Be angry, but do not sin; do not let the sun set on your anger.' },
            prov15_1: { r: ['箴言 15:1', 'Proverbs 15:1'], zh: '柔和的回答，能消除憤怒；惡言惡語，只會激起怒氣。', en: 'A gentle answer turns away wrath, but a harsh word stirs up anger.' },
            cor10_13: { r: ['格林多前書 10:13', '1 Corinthians 10:13'], zh: '天主是忠信的，決不許你們受那超過你們能力的試探；在試探時，他必給你們開一條出路，叫你們能夠忍受得住。', en: 'God is faithful and will not let you be tempted beyond your strength; with the temptation he will also provide a way out, so that you may be able to bear it.' },
            jn1_9:    { r: ['若望一書 1:9', '1 John 1:9'], zh: '我們若承認自己的罪過，天主是忠信正義的，必赦免我們的罪過，洗淨我們各種的不義。', en: 'If we acknowledge our sins, he is faithful and just and will forgive our sins and cleanse us from every wrongdoing.' },
            mt26_41:  { r: ['瑪竇福音 26:41', 'Matthew 26:41'], zh: '你們醒寤祈禱，免得陷於誘惑；你們的心神固然切願，肉身卻是軟弱的。', en: 'Watch and pray that you may not undergo the test. The spirit is willing, but the flesh is weak.' },
            eccl4_9:  { r: ['訓道篇 4:9-10', 'Ecclesiastes 4:9-10'], zh: '兩個人比一個人好，因為他們勞苦會有好報酬；如果一個跌倒，另一個可以扶起他的同伴。', en: 'Two are better than one, because they get a good return for their toil. If one falls, the other can lift up his companion.' },
            prov27_17:{ r: ['箴言 27:17', 'Proverbs 27:17'], zh: '鐵磨鐵，磨出刃來；人與人相處，也磨礪出智慧。', en: 'Iron sharpens iron, and one man sharpens another.' },
            mt18_20:  { r: ['瑪竇福音 18:20', 'Matthew 18:20'], zh: '因為哪裡有兩三個人因我的名聚在一起，我就在他們中間。', en: 'Where two or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of them.' },
            jn20_29:  { r: ['若望福音 20:29', 'John 20:29'], zh: '你因為看見了我才信；沒有看見而信的人是有福的。', en: 'Have you come to believe because you have seen me? Blessed are those who have not seen and have believed.' },
            mt14_31:  { r: ['瑪竇福音 14:31', 'Matthew 14:31'], zh: '耶穌立即伸手拉住他，對他說：「小信的人哪，你為什麼懷疑呢？」', en: 'Immediately Jesus stretched out his hand and caught him, saying to him, “O you of little faith, why did you doubt?”' },
            lk17_5:   { r: ['路加福音 17:5', 'Luke 17:5'], zh: '宗徒們對主說：「請增加我們的信德！」', en: 'The apostles said to the Lord, “Increase our faith.”' },
            ps34_19:  { r: ['聖詠 34:19', 'Psalm 34:19'], zh: '上主接近心靈破碎的人，拯救神魂痛悔的人。', en: 'The LORD is close to the brokenhearted and saves those who are crushed in spirit.' },
            mt5_4:    { r: ['瑪竇福音 5:4', 'Matthew 5:4'], zh: '哀慟的人是有福的，因為他們要受安慰。', en: 'Blessed are they who mourn, for they will be comforted.' },
            jn11_25:  { r: ['若望福音 11:25', 'John 11:25'], zh: '耶穌對她說：「復活和生命就是我；信從我的人，即使死了，也要活著。」', en: 'Jesus said to her, “I am the resurrection and the life; whoever believes in me, even if he dies, will live.”' },
            rev21_4:  { r: ['默示錄 21:4', 'Revelation 21:4'], zh: '他要擦去他們眼上的一切淚痕，以後再沒有死亡，再沒有悲傷，沒有哀號，也沒有痛苦，因為先前的事已成過去。', en: 'He will wipe every tear from their eyes, and there shall be no more death or mourning, wailing or pain, for the old order has passed away.' },
            th5_16:   { r: ['得撒洛尼前書 5:16-18', '1 Thessalonians 5:16-18'], zh: '你們要常常喜樂，不斷地祈禱，凡事感恩，因為這是天主在基督耶穌內對你們所有的旨意。', en: 'Rejoice always, pray without ceasing, give thanks in all circumstances; for this is the will of God for you in Christ Jesus.' },
            ps103_2:  { r: ['聖詠 103:2', 'Psalm 103:2'], zh: '我的靈魂，你要讚美上主，不要忘記他的一切恩惠。', en: 'Bless the LORD, my soul, and do not forget all his gifts.' },
            prov3_5:  { r: ['箴言 3:5-6', 'Proverbs 3:5-6'], zh: '你要全心依賴上主，不要倚恃你自己的聰明；在你一切的道路上，要認識他，他必指引你的路徑。', en: 'Trust in the LORD with all your heart, on your own intelligence do not rely; in all your ways be mindful of him, and he will make straight your paths.' },
            ps119_105:{ r: ['聖詠 119:105', 'Psalm 119:105'], zh: '你的話是我腳前的明燈，是我路上的光亮。', en: 'Your word is a lamp for my feet, a light for my path.' },
            jas1_5:   { r: ['雅各伯書 1:5', 'James 1:5'], zh: '你們中若有人缺少智慧，應向天主求，他必賜給他，因為天主厚施於眾人，並不斥責人。', en: 'If any of you lacks wisdom, he should ask God, who gives to all generously and ungrudgingly, and he will be given it.' },
            mt6_14:   { r: ['瑪竇福音 6:14-15', 'Matthew 6:14-15'], zh: '如果你們寬恕別人的過犯，你們的天父也必寬恕你們；如果你們不寬恕別人，你們的天父也必不寬恕你們的過犯。', en: 'If you forgive others their transgressions, your heavenly Father will forgive you. But if you do not forgive others, neither will your Father forgive your transgressions.' },
            col3_13:  { r: ['哥羅森書 3:13', 'Colossians 3:13'], zh: '你們要互相忍耐；如果彼此間有什麼怨恨，要互相寬恕；主怎樣寬恕了你們，你們也該怎樣寬恕。', en: 'Bear with one another and forgive one another, if one has a grievance against another; as the Lord has forgiven you, so must you also do.' },
            mt18_21:  { r: ['瑪竇福音 18:21-22', 'Matthew 18:21-22'], zh: '伯多祿前來問耶穌：「主，如果我的弟兄得罪我，我該寬恕他幾次呢？七次嗎？」耶穌對他說：「我不對你說七次，而是七十個七次。」', en: 'Peter approached Jesus and asked, “Lord, if my brother sins against me, how often must I forgive him? As many as seven times?” Jesus answered, “I say to you, not seven times but seventy-seven times.”' },
            lk11_9:   { r: ['路加福音 11:9-10', 'Luke 11:9-10'], zh: '我也對你們說：你們求，必給你們；你們找，必找到；你們敲，必給你們開。', en: 'And I say to you, ask and it will be given to you; seek and you will find; knock and the door will be opened to you.' },
            mt6_6:    { r: ['瑪竇福音 6:6', 'Matthew 6:6'], zh: '你祈禱時，要進入你的內室，關上門，向在暗中的父祈禱；你的父在暗中看見，必要報答你。', en: 'When you pray, go to your inner room, close the door and pray to your Father in secret. And your Father who sees in secret will repay you.' },
            rom8_26:  { r: ['羅馬書 8:26', 'Romans 8:26'], zh: '同樣，聖神也扶助我們的軟弱，因為我們不知道我們當怎樣祈求才對；但聖神親自以無可言喻的歎息，代我們轉求。', en: 'The Spirit too comes to the aid of our weakness; for we do not know how to pray as we ought, but the Spirit himself intercedes with inexpressible groanings.' },
            gal6_9:   { r: ['迦拉達書 6:9', 'Galatians 6:9'], zh: '我們行善不要厭倦，如果我們不灰心，到了時候，必要收穫。', en: 'Let us not grow weary of doing good, for in due time we shall reap our harvest, if we do not give up.' },
            is40_31:  { r: ['依撒意亞 40:31', 'Isaiah 40:31'], zh: '但那些仰望上主的，必獲得新的力量，要像鷹隼一樣展翅上騰；他們奔跑，也不困倦，他們行走，也不疲乏。', en: 'They that hope in the LORD will renew their strength, they will soar on eagles\' wings; they will run and not grow weary, walk and not grow faint.' },
            lam3_22:  { r: ['哀歌 3:22-23', 'Lamentations 3:22-23'], zh: '上主的慈愛永不斷絕，他的憐憫永不窮盡；每天早晨，都是新的；你的忠信多麼廣大！', en: 'The steadfast love of the LORD never ceases, his mercies never come to an end; they are new every morning; great is your faithfulness.' },
            mt5_16:   { r: ['瑪竇福音 5:14,16', 'Matthew 5:14,16'], zh: '你們是世界的光……你們的光也該這樣照在人前，使他們看見你們的善行，光榮你們在天之父。', en: 'You are the light of the world … Your light must shine before others, that they may see your good deeds and glorify your Father in heaven.' },
            jer29_11: { r: ['耶肋米亞 29:11', 'Jeremiah 29:11'], zh: '因為我知道我對你們所懷的計劃──上主的斷語──是平安，而不是災禍的計劃，為給你們一個有希望的未來。', en: 'For I know well the plans I have in mind for you, says the LORD, plans for your welfare and not for woe, so as to give you a future of hope.' },
            mt6_33:   { r: ['瑪竇福音 6:33', 'Matthew 6:33'], zh: '你們要先尋求天主的國和他的義德，這一切也要加給你們。', en: 'Seek first the kingdom of God and his righteousness, and all these things will be given you besides.' },
            heb13_5:  { r: ['希伯來書 13:5', 'Hebrews 13:5'], zh: '你們不要貪愛錢財，要以現有的為滿足，因為天主親自說過：「我決不離棄你，也決不拋棄你。」', en: 'Let your life be free from love of money; be content with what you have, for he has said, “I will never forsake you or abandon you.”' },
            mt7_24:   { r: ['瑪竇福音 7:24-25', 'Matthew 7:24-25'], zh: '凡聽了我這些話而實行的，就好比一個聰明人，把自己的房屋建築在磐石上。雨淋，水沖，風吹，撞擊那房屋，房屋仍不倒塌，因為它建築在磐石上。', en: 'Everyone who listens to these words of mine and acts on them will be like a wise man who built his house on rock. The rain fell, the floods came, and the winds blew and buffeted the house. But it did not collapse; it had been set solidly on rock.' },
            mt16_18:  { r: ['瑪竇福音 16:18', 'Matthew 16:18'], zh: '你是伯多祿，在這磐石上我要建立我的教會，陰間的門決不能戰勝她。', en: 'You are Peter, and upon this rock I will build my Church, and the gates of the netherworld shall not prevail against it.' },
            ps18_3:   { r: ['聖詠 18:3', 'Psalm 18:2'], zh: '上主是我的磐石，我的堡壘，我的救主。', en: 'The LORD is my rock, my fortress, my deliverer.' },
            mt1_24:   { r: ['瑪竇福音 1:24', 'Matthew 1:24'], zh: '若瑟一醒來，就照上主天使所吩咐的做了，把自己的妻子接到家裡。', en: 'When Joseph awoke, he did as the angel of the Lord had commanded him and took his wife into his home.' },
            mt2_14:   { r: ['瑪竇福音 2:14', 'Matthew 2:14'], zh: '若瑟便起來，夜間帶著嬰兒和他的母親，退避到埃及去了。', en: 'Joseph rose and took the child and his mother by night and departed for Egypt.' }
        };

