                'Catholics believe Jesus Christ is the Son of God, truly God and truly man. Conceived by the Holy Spirit and born of the Virgin Mary, he grew up in Judea and began his public ministry at about thirty: proclaiming the Gospel of the kingdom, healing the sick, forgiving sinners and calling the Twelve Apostles.',
                'He suffered and died on the cross, rose on the third day, ascended into heaven and will come again. Through his death and resurrection sin and death are conquered, humanity is reconciled with God and eternal life is opened to us.',
